# iOS Testing Task

## Goal

Keep Swift tool ownership, project generation, simulator selection, XCTest evidence, and user-data isolation explicit and reproducible. Prefer `swift-format` as the sole formatting owner. SwiftLint is optional; its formatting-style rules can overlap or conflict with `swift-format`, so either keep SwiftLint semantic-only or deliberately disable `swift-format` before assigning formatting ownership to SwiftLint.

## Test Commands

```bash
./scripts/test.mjs unit
./scripts/test.mjs ui
./scripts/test.mjs all
./scripts/test.mjs selected {{ swift_unit_test_target | default('AppTests') }}/ExampleTests
```

All local XCTest commands resolve the fixed simulator through `scripts/simulator.mjs`. CI must set `{{ swift_test_destination_env | default('APP_TEST_DESTINATION') }}` to an explicit destination already installed on the runner.

`xcodebuild build-for-testing` proves that the app and test bundles compile; it is not evidence that tests ran or passed. Reports must distinguish `built`, `test bundle compiled`, and `tests passed`.

## Deterministic UI Journeys

Before adding a UI journey to the scheme-level suite:

1. Inject deterministic fixture state through launch arguments or environment.
2. Isolate persistence, preferences, accounts, files, and network responses from developer data.
3. Add stable accessibility identifiers only when semantic labels are insufficient.
4. Assert visible behavior rather than implementation details or fixed delays.
5. Prove the journey through `xcodebuild` on the fixed simulator and in the full gate.
6. Add or update its broad XCTest impact area.

Keep manual device checks for system-owned UI, permissions, hardware, real cloud assets, performance, and visual qualities that semantic assertions cannot establish.

{% if include_xctest_impact_selection | default(false) -%}
## Changed-Scope Impact Areas

`scripts/xctest-impact-rules.mjs` maps durable source responsibility patterns to focused XCTest source patterns. It deliberately starts empty: add the first rule with the first product source and focused test, then keep every product source, configured resource, test-support source, and XCTestCase covered.

Run:

```bash
node scripts/validate-xctest-impact-rules.mjs --strict
./scripts/validate-changed-scope.mjs --skip-ui-tests
```

`--skip-ui-tests` is an explicit local-iteration choice, not UI evidence. Run the relevant UI class/method or omit the option when the change needs UI proof. Full finalization remains exhaustive.{% endif %}

## Project And Simulator Changes

- Edit `{{ swift_project_spec_path | default('project.yml') }}`, never generated `.xcodeproj` internals.
- Regenerate after changing targets, packages, settings, schemes, or source membership.
- Keep `Package.resolved` tracked.
- Create or update the fixed simulator only through an explicit decision and `./scripts/simulator.mjs create`.
